  │ [0m[38;2;177;185;249msearch[0m    │ One node read per level, so about log n reads for n keys                       │
  ├───────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ [0m[38;2;177;185;249minsert[0m    │ The cost of a search, plus a split at each full node on the way back up        │
  ├───────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ [0m[38;2;177;185;249mdelete[0m    │ The cost of a search, plus a borrow or merge at each node left under half full │
  └───────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  A B-tree buys its shallow shape with a little extra work on writes, and that is a good trade whenever reads are slow.

